hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16736","He said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from al-Fadl ibn Amr ibn Umayya, from his father, he said: I heard men narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When the slave woman is freed, she has the choice so long as he has not had intercourse with her; if she wishes she leaves him, and if he has intercourse with her, she has no choice and cannot leave him."
"16737","He said: Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Umayya al-Damri, he said: I heard men from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave woman is freed while she is under a slave, her affair is in her hand; if she remains until he has intercourse with her, she is his wife and cannot leave him."
